00:53.277 --> 00:56.220
the friendliest manner.

00:56.220 --> 00:57.854
Anyway, if we read the description, it says

00:57.854 --> 01:00.390
this command creates an empty git repo

01:00.390 --> 01:02.880
basically a .git directory

01:02.880 --> 01:05.250
with sub directories for blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.

01:05.250 --> 01:09.180
Hmm. So it creates a directory called .git.

01:09.180 --> 01:11.700
Now, if you know anything about hidden folders

01:11.700 --> 01:15.960
and hidden files, you'll know they all start with a dot.

01:15.960 --> 01:19.260
And there is a hidden folder that we're just not seeing

01:19.260 --> 01:21.690
in this directory where I ran git init.

01:21.690 --> 01:24.690
If I type out not KS, LS.

01:24.690 --> 01:26.040
I don't see anything.

01:26.040 --> 01:28.909
But if I use the -a flag, that's one way of

01:28.909 --> 01:32.250
of seeing all, I think it's, I don't know if it's A for all.

01:32.250 --> 01:33.600
That's what I tell myself.

01:33.600 --> 01:36.533
All files hidden and non-hidden.

01:36.533 --> 01:39.433
Now we see this folder .git.

01:39.433 --> 01:42.352
So if I wanted to, you know, I could look at that.

01:42.352 --> 01:44.580
We don't need to touch it or do anything in there

01:44.580 --> 01:46.860
but this is what we just initialized.

01:46.860 --> 01:50.703
So if I delete this, my git history is gone.

01:50.703 --> 01:54.390
Now we can, you know, back it up and put it on GitHub

01:54.390 --> 01:55.920
and stuff like that once we get there.

01:55.920 --> 01:59.220
But for now, just to prove this, I'm just gonna back out

01:59.220 --> 02:00.053
of here.

02:00.053 --> 02:02.280
I type git status, as we already have seen.

02:02.280 --> 02:05.340
It tells me git stuff, I'm in a repo.

02:05.340 --> 02:08.296
If I back out one more level, just to be clear, now I'm,

02:08.296 --> 02:10.740
I'm outside of this folder.

02:10.740 --> 02:12.273
If I run git status,

02:13.140 --> 02:14.940
not a get repo.

02:14.940 --> 02:18.060
Go back into my first novel, get status.

02:18.060 --> 02:22.590
Okay. So if I remove that folder, rm-rf

02:22.590 --> 02:23.820
you don't need to do this.

02:23.820 --> 02:26.160
This is gonna delete the entire git history

02:26.160 --> 02:27.240
for this project.

02:27.240 --> 02:30.723
If I do that, I type git status.

02:31.830 --> 02:34.050
I'm back to not being in a repository.

02:34.050 --> 02:37.470
So that .git folder is where all the git stuff occurs.

02:37.470 --> 02:38.975
That's, that's what holds it all.

02:38.975 --> 02:42.630
So I'm gonna run git init again, which is, it's okay here

02:42.630 --> 02:46.410
